Each new Python process pays three to five seconds to load the embedding model before its first search. kosha daemon loads it once and then answers requests read from standard input, one JSON object per line, writing one JSON line per answer. It prints {"ok": true, "status": "ready"} when it is ready.
kosha daemon
Each request names a command and its arguments:
{"cmd": "context", "args": {"q": "embed a query", "limit": 10}}
{"ok": true, "result": [...]}

{"cmd": "short_path", "args": {"src": "kosha.core.Kosha.sync", "tgt": "litesearch.core.search"}}
{"ok": true, "result": [...]}
A failed request returns {"ok": false, "error": "..."}. The commands are sync, status, context, repo_context, env_context, ni, neighbors, short_path, top_nodes, public_api, api_call_paths, dep_stack, where_to_add and nuke, with the same arguments as the Kosha methods of those names. ni takes mod_name.

The graph on a Kosha
Kosha.graph opens .kosha/graph.db in the repository, once per Kosha object. graphdb, gn and ge expose the database and its node and edge tables for direct queries. ni, neighbors, short_path and short_paths are the CodeGraph methods of the same names. ni is node_info. On a Kosha called k, k.ni('fastcore.basics.merge') returns the node row with its callers, callees and co-dispatch peers.



Kosha.short_paths
def short_paths():
The graph’s short_paths among a list of nodes.





Kosha.short_path
def short_path():
The graph’s short_path between two nodes.





Kosha.neighbors
def neighbors():
The graph’s neighbors: every node within depth edges.





Kosha.ni
def ni():
The graph’s node_info: a node’s row plus its callers, callees and co-dispatch peers.





Kosha.ge
def ge():
The graph_edges table, for direct queries.





Kosha.gn
def gn():
The graph_nodes table, for direct queries.





Kosha.graphdb
